'''Llaragón''' ({{literal translation|place of hearth}}; {{langx|kp|Porã-Rekó|4=beautiful dwelling}}) is a [[regions of Balisca|region]] in central [[Bayara]] located in the foothills of the [[Matarrañya|Matarrañya / Cañadapirén]]. It consists of {{W|prairie}}, {{W|savanna}}, {{W|riparian forest}}, {{W|marsh}}, several types of seasonal {{W|vernal pool}}s, [[w:Channel (geography)|channels]] and large lakes.

Rice farming in this area produces 20% of Balisca's national crop. Significant portions of the region are protected for wildlife and habitat, and there are several ongoing projects aimed at {{W|rewilding}} and {{W|Restoration ecology|restoring the floodplains}}. The region's floodplains are of significance to the wider [[Western Plains (Balisca)|Western Plains]] ecoregion. 

